{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Root.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Root.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"root root","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Root.md","fileName":"Root.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Root","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Exponents and Roots]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Exponents and Roots","Square Root","Cube Root","Irrational Number","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Root.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Root.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"root root","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Root.md","fileName":"Root.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Root","heading":"Root","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An (m)th root reverses an (m)th power. If (a=b^m), then (b) is an (m)th root of (a), written\n\n$$b=\\sqrt[m]{a}.$$\n\nThe number (m\\geq2) is the root's index and (a) is the quantity under the root symbol. An index of two is normally omitted, producing a [[Square Root]], while an index of three gives a [[Cube Root]]. Root extraction can produce an [[Irrational Number]] even when the original value is a natural number.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Exponents and Roots","Square Root","Cube Root","Irrational Number","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Root.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Root.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"root root","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Root.md","fileName":"Root.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Root","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Exponents and Roots","Square Root","Cube Root","Irrational Number","algebraessen